<h1>Lisa Nee</h1>
<p>Cardiologist and former ICU nurse. Candidate for mayor of Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p>Interventional cardiologist, former ICU nurse, and the whistleblower on unnecessary heart procedures at the Hines VA hospital; 59, grew up in Humboldt Park and lives on the North Side. A first-time candidate who filed 31,000 signatures.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.lisaneeforchicago.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website (lisaneeforchicago.com)</a></p>
<h2>What sets them apart</h2>
<p>Property taxes: The one candidate who says an increase is not completely off the table. Holberg, Kelly, and Kitover would freeze or lower them.</p>
<p>The pitch: A cardiologist and hospital whistleblower who has never run for office.</p>
<p>Not published: No platform page. The site names three themes, affordability, safety, and fiscal responsibility, with no policy behind them yet.</p>
<h2>Where they split from the field</h2>
<p>Property taxes: An increase is not off the table. Freeze or lower them: Kelly, Holberg, and Kitover. Hold the city&#39;s levy flat: Giannoulias.</p>
<h2>In their words</h2>
<ul>
<li>Will not promise that a property tax increase is off the table. <q>I&#39;m never going to lie to people and say that it&#39;s completely off the table.</q> (<a href="https://www.pbs.org/video/mayoral-candidate-lisa-nee-on-plans-for-chicago-zluusq/" rel="nofollow noopener">WTTW Chicago Tonight, July 29, 2026, on property taxes (auto-transcript)</a>)</li>
<li>Runs as an outsider who has watched systems fail people and is done accepting it. <q>I&#39;m running because I believe we deserve a city where public service actually serves the public</q> (<a href="https://www.nbcchicago.com/news/local/chicago-politics/chicago-cardiologist-enters-2027-mayoral-race/3958259/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign statement, July 7, 2026 (NBC Chicago)</a>)</li>
<li>Speed up the permit process and run the mayor&#39;s office as a collaborator. <q>The role of the mayor should be collaborating.</q> (<a href="https://www.pbs.org/video/mayoral-candidate-lisa-nee-on-plans-for-chicago-zluusq/" rel="nofollow noopener">WTTW Chicago Tonight, July 29, 2026 (auto-transcript)</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Campaign money</h2>
<ul>
<li>Committee: Lisa Nee for Chicago</li>
<li>Raised: $139K</li>
<li>Spent: $89K</li>
<li>Cash on hand: $51K</li>
<li>Since the committee formed July 8, 2026, through Sept. 30. Includes a $50,000 loan from the candidate. <a href="https://elections.il.gov/CampaignDisclosure/CommitteeDetail.aspx?id=41265" rel="nofollow noopener">Source</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Money figures are each committee&#39;s quarterly reports to the Illinois State Board of Elections: spent is total expenditures from January 1 to September 30, 2026 (or since the committee formed), cash is funds available on September 30.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
<p>Not listed in the ChicagoSpeaks poll, Sept. 2026 (Mansueto Institute / NORC). 0.0 points of support per $1 million spent.</p>
<h2>On money</h2>
<p>Would grow the tax base and add transparency and accountability to the budget, and says she will not promise that property taxes are completely off the table.</p>
<ul>
<li><q>I think you have to grow the tax base.</q> (<a href="https://www.pbs.org/video/mayoral-candidate-lisa-nee-on-plans-for-chicago-zluusq/" rel="nofollow noopener">WTTW Chicago Tonight, July 29, 2026 (auto-transcript)</a>)</li>
<li><q>I&#39;m never going to lie to people and say that it&#39;s completely off the table.</q> (<a href="https://www.pbs.org/video/mayoral-candidate-lisa-nee-on-plans-for-chicago-zluusq/" rel="nofollow noopener">WTTW Chicago Tonight, July 29, 2026, on property taxes (auto-transcript)</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pizza</h2>
<p>No position on record.</p>
<h2>Also on the record</h2>
<ul>
<li>Ran Division I track at Loyola, and lives with her husband, children, and two dogs. (<a href="https://chicago.suntimes.com/city-hall/2026/07/07/dr-lisa-nee-joins-growing-field-of-candidates-for-chicago-mayor" rel="nofollow noopener">chicago.suntimes.com</a>)</li>
